# Material-slot demo asset for scenes/material_slots.luz.
#
# Three slots share one mesh:
#   Bulb  - the bright lamp face (emissive in the scene)
#   Shade  - the lamp shade shell (diffuse)
#   Frame  - the supporting bracket (dark metal-ish)
# The two instances in the scene bind these slots to different materials.
#
# A mobile lamp stand: a tilted shade quad, a glowing underside panel and a
# thin bracket. Faces are named through "usemtl", which is all Luz needs; the
# referenced MTL file (if any) is never read.
v -0.60 1.40 -0.60
v  0.60 1.40 -0.60
v  0.80 1.60  0.60
v -0.80 1.60  0.60
v -0.55 1.34 -0.55
v  0.55 1.34 -0.55
v  0.62 1.34  0.55
v -0.62 1.34  0.55
v -0.10 0.00 -0.10
v  0.10 0.00 -0.10
v  0.10 0.00  0.10
v -0.10 0.00  0.10
v -0.06 1.34 -0.06
v  0.06 1.34 -0.06
v  0.06 1.34  0.06
v -0.06 1.34  0.06
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 0.0 1.0
usemtl Frame
f 1 2 3 4
usemtl Shade
f 5 6 7 8
usemtl Bulb
f 5 6 14 13
f 6 7 15 14
f 7 8 16 15
f 8 5 13 16
usemtl Frame
f 9 10 14 13
f 10 11 15 14
f 11 12 16 15
f 12 9 13 16
f 9 10 11 12
